comments.body:
In practice, the client's IP address is often used for negative authorization decision:

* Reddit kicks me when I try to anonymously browse it from a VPS IP address;
* Google's Captcha turns extra paranoid when you are coming from a Tor IP address (you spend 5 minutes filling horrible super slow Captchas and it often ends up failing anyway);
* many websites won't allow you to create an account at all when your are coming from a Tor IP address;
* many media content providers will refuse to serve your things based on IP-address based geolocation.
